# POST /seed — step 1: parse the request.
#
# /seed exists ONLY to make this example self-contained: it provisions a
# LOCAL IMAP account (served by `txco dev --imap` on 127.0.0.1:1143) and
# drops a message into its INBOX, so the source has a real mailbox to
# watch without a third-party provider. In a real deployment the mailbox
# is Fastmail/Gmail/Dovecot and there is no /seed — you only declare the
# source and store its password.
#
# No body is needed. The FIRST seed creates the account and answers with
# its password, once — the chassis generates every password (it carries
# the credential's id). Store that value as the secret the source
# references (PONY_MAILBOX): the source logs in with the secret, so it
# must be the account's password. Later seeds only add messages. Mark
# that a seed request is in flight.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.method == "POST" && @web.req.url.path == "/seed"
  EMIT ._seed = &try_json(&b64decode(@web.req.body)),
       ._seed_req = true
